  "published": "2026-09-24T19:41:49.183Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "New LinqContraband.Scan tool: run dnx LinqContraband.Scan (or dotnet tool install -g LinqContraband.Scan) to scan any solution without adding this package. It prints the rules that fired ranked by severity and count, the most affected files and a link to each rule, and writes a SARIF report for GitHub code scanning, including EF Core's EF1002/EF1003, which LC018 and LC034 defer to. Fixes: LC001 trusts pgvector functions and adds a trusted_namespaces option; LC007 no longer reports hierarchies walked one level per query; LC040 and LC045 no longer hang the build on query = query.Where(...); LC033 now reports on real .NET 8+ projects; LC023 keeps reporting in projects with more than 64 source files; LC030 long_lived_types accepts a comma-separated list; LC009 and LC031 report a double materialization once; LC029 no longer reports Select(v => v!) over nullable elements. Code fixes: LC009 places AsNoTracking() after FromSql*; LC008, LC012, LC041 and LC027 add the using or namespace they need; LC043, LC001, LC012, LC020 and LC023 work on chained receivers; LC002, LC006, LC008, LC009, LC021, LC026 and LC029 work when the reported call is an argument. The README's build guidance and LC038/LC042 threshold examples are corrected. Full notes: https://github.com/georgepwall1991/LinqContraband/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md",
